Warning



By default, the first page is always “plain”, and won’t reflect the changes you make to headers etc. This can be appealing or not. To change it, add \thispagestyle{fancy} to the affected page.
The very first line of your code may have twosided as an option turned on. Unfortunately (or perhaps fortunately) this doesn’t affect what is “left” or “right” on odd/even numbered pages; there are ways to add “inner” header and “outer” header marks but that’s more than we need right now.
